# ThreadSanitizer suppressions — third-party only.
#
# This job exists to check ONE thing: the background recovery, which is the
# only place Sable hands document data across a thread boundary. Nothing here
# may suppress a report whose stack touches Sable's own code.
#
# Each entry names a library and the report kind, so a genuine race in the save
# path can never be hidden by a rule aimed at somebody else's locking.

# libdbus takes two of its own mutexes in opposite orders on different paths.
# TSan reports it as a POTENTIAL deadlock; the stack contains only
# libdbus-1.so.3 and libc.so.6, no Sable frames. Reached because SDL probes for
# a GPU device at startup, which brings in desktop integration the self-test
# did not previously touch. Not ours to fix, and not something we can avoid
# without giving up the device probe.
deadlock:libdbus-1

# SDL's own initialisation and teardown of desktop-integration threads.
race:libSDL3
deadlock:libSDL3
